00:06:08 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :Deewiant: Going east, starting at the beginning of the line, considering x as a nop, with 1 on the stack, xk goes:
00:06:16 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :(where _x_ denotes ip is here)
00:06:20 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :_x_k --> execute x
00:06:27 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :x_k_ --> execute x from start of line
00:06:30 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :_x_k --> execute k
00:06:32 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :*x
00:06:33 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :right?
00:06:38 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :as in, k wraps around
00:06:39 :Deewiant!~deewiant@cs186230.pp.htv.fi PRIVMSG #esoteric :"From start of line"?
00:06:41 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :Deewiant: Yes.
00:06:43 :Deewiant!~deewiant@cs186230.pp.htv.fi PRIVMSG #esoteric :Everything wraps around
00:06:53 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :Deewiant: So k wraps around to find x, runs it, and then the IP wraps around to x.
00:06:54 :Deewiant!~deewiant@cs186230.pp.htv.fi PRIVMSG #esoteric :But note that you are executing the x at the k
00:06:54 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :Right.
00:07:01 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :Deewiant: Er.
00:07:07 :Deewiant!~deewiant@cs186230.pp.htv.fi PRIVMSG #esoteric :This matters for instructions that take the IP's position into account
00:07:10 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :Deewiant: Does that means that "kj" moves down from k? :-D
00:07:12 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :Awesome.
00:07:26 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :Deewiant: What does 11kkj do?
00:07:28 :Deewiant!~deewiant@cs186230.pp.htv.fi PRIVMSG #esoteric :Mycology is pretty nitpicky about k, don't worry
00:07:33 :Deewiant!~deewiant@cs186230.pp.htv.fi PRIVMSG #esoteric :Don't ask me about nested k.
00:07:33 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :JUST OUT OF CURIOSITY
00:07:35 :Deewiant!~deewiant@cs186230.pp.htv.fi PRIVMSG #esoteric :Just don't.
00:07:37 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :Deewiant: I'M ASKING
00:07:43 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :IIIIII'M ASKING
00:07:44 :Deewiant!~deewiant@cs186230.pp.htv.fi PRIVMSG #esoteric :Vorpal disagrees with me on it anyway.
00:07:50 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :Well let me try and work it out myself.
00:07:59 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :Let's say 11kkx, where x does nothing.
00:08:07 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :So.
00:08:17 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :left-k goes to execute right-k.
00:08:32 :Deewiant!~deewiant@cs186230.pp.htv.fi PRIVMSG #esoteric :In my defence, cfunge special-cases nested k and I don't.
00:08:32 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :k is defined as being based on the "path of the IP".
00:08:37 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :So k finds the right k again.
00:08:39 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :And executes it.
00:08:42 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :Right k finds the right k again.
00:08:45 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :And executes it.
00:08:54 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :Aaaand it's an infinite loop taking 0 ticks.
00:08:54 :Deewiant!~deewiant@cs186230.pp.htv.fi PRIVMSG #esoteric :Right k doesn't find itself.
00:08:57 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :ORLY?
00:09:02 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :"Then it finds the next instruction in Funge-space in the path of the IP (note that this cannot be a marker such as space or ;),"
00:09:08 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :The IP is still on the first k.
00:09:12 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :The next instruction after the IP is the second k.
00:09:15 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :So the second k finds the second k.
00:09:19 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :And executes it.
00:09:26 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :Which actually pops *0* off the stack!
00:09:30 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :Because now we have no stack left.
00:09:33 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :And so it skips the x.
00:09:38 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :So 11kxy goes to y after 0 ticks.
00:09:40 :Vorpal!~AnMaster@unaffiliated/anmaster PRIVMSG #esoteric :elliott, nested k is an issue
00:09:42 :Deewiant!~deewiant@cs186230.pp.htv.fi PRIVMSG #esoteric :I'm too tired to think about this now, do whatever you like. :-P
00:09:42 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :Well, after 1 tick.
00:09:45 :Vorpal!~AnMaster@unaffiliated/anmaster PRIVMSG #esoteric :read the code if you care
00:09:51 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :Deewiant: Nonono, I just came up with a new opinion.
00:09:55 :Vorpal!~AnMaster@unaffiliated/anmaster PRIVMSG #esoteric :I don't really care about it. No one uses it anyway!
00:10:03 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :Deewiant: 11kxy.
00:10:08 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :erm
00:10:10 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :11kkxy
00:10:11 :Vorpal!~AnMaster@unaffiliated/anmaster PRIVMSG #esoteric :elliott, there is a test case in tests/ in cfunge for it iirc
00:10:13 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :Stack = 1 1.
00:10:14 :Vorpal!~AnMaster@unaffiliated/anmaster PRIVMSG #esoteric :check there if you care
00:10:16 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :k pops first stack.
00:10:17 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :Stack = 1.
00:10:22 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :It goes to execute the second k.
00:10:24 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :k pops first stack.
00:10:27 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :Stack = 0 0 0 0 0 0 ...
00:10:31 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :The IP is still on the first k.
00:10:39 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :The next instruction in Funge-space in the IP's path is the second k, therefore.
00:10:40 :Vorpal!~AnMaster@unaffiliated/anmaster PRIVMSG #esoteric :elliott, what about 3 nested k?
00:10:45 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :It goes to execute the second k.
00:10:49 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :The second k pops off 0.
00:10:53 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :Since it's 0, it skips the second k.
00:10:57 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :It goes on to x.
00:10:58 :Vorpal!~AnMaster@unaffiliated/anmaster PRIVMSG #esoteric :night! →
