07:03:42 :nrkn!3ceaa170@gateway/web/freenode/ip.60.234.161.112 PRIVMSG #esoteric :So I looked at golfscript, what other langs are good for golf? Making my own, some good stuff in golfscript but I feel can be improved upon for terseness. Au fait with lisp, perl etc., still too verbose. Also trying to do something that's reasonably mnemonic, ie short but not toooo cryptic
07:06:24 :fizzie!fis@iris.zem.fi PRIVMSG #esoteric :There's goruby, but that's I guess mostly just a identifier-shortened Ruby.
07:06:25 :quintopia!~quintopia@unaffiliated/quintopia PRIVMSG #esoteric :nrkn: take a look a j
07:06:34 :fizzie!fis@iris.zem.fi PRIVMSG #esoteric :And of course J, yes.
07:07:03 :nrkn!3ceaa170@gateway/web/freenode/ip.60.234.161.112 PRIVMSG #esoteric :J seems like a terrible thing to google haha. I'll try esolang first?
07:07:11 :fizzie!fis@iris.zem.fi PRIVMSG #esoteric :And FlogScript.
07:07:14 :oerjan!oerjan@tyrell.nvg.ntnu.no JOIN :#esoteric
07:07:16 :nrkn!3ceaa170@gateway/web/freenode/ip.60.234.161.112 PRIVMSG #esoteric :And goruby. Know a bit of Ruby
07:07:28 :nrkn!3ceaa170@gateway/web/freenode/ip.60.234.161.112 PRIVMSG #esoteric :OK FlogScript, will look at
07:07:30 :nrkn!3ceaa170@gateway/web/freenode/ip.60.234.161.112 PRIVMSG #esoteric :Brb
07:08:44 :quintopia!~quintopia@unaffiliated/quintopia PRIVMSG #esoteric :z80 also seems to result in small bytecodes for a lot of things :P
07:09:45 :fizzie!fis@iris.zem.fi PRIVMSG #esoteric :http://golf.shinh.org/lranking.rb may give some sort of a golfability indication, though I think it's more about language popularity.
07:10:15 :asiekierka!~asiekierk@178235033089.elblag.vectranet.pl JOIN :#esoteric
07:10:45 :fizzie!fis@iris.zem.fi PRIVMSG #esoteric :Would be more useful if it were sorted by the "Avg." column.
07:11:25 :quintopia!~quintopia@unaffiliated/quintopia PRIVMSG #esoteric :would it
07:11:37 :quintopia!~quintopia@unaffiliated/quintopia PRIVMSG #esoteric :i feel like people use the best language for each problem
07:11:45 :quintopia!~quintopia@unaffiliated/quintopia PRIVMSG #esoteric :and don't use it if it's gonna be long
07:12:29 :fizzie!fis@iris.zem.fi PRIVMSG #esoteric :Well, or alternatively choose only moderately popular languages and take the set of problems solved in all of them.
07:13:27 :quintopia!~quintopia@unaffiliated/quintopia PRIVMSG #esoteric :some people just always use the same language tho
07:13:40 :fizzie!fis@iris.zem.fi PRIVMSG #esoteric :I always just use Befunge. :p
07:14:07 :nrkn!3ceaa170@gateway/web/freenode/ip.60.234.161.112 PRIVMSG #esoteric :Yeah if it's a matter of how many chars you use measured in bytes you have so many operators available where in unicode it's only one byte, provided you use the letter chars (including accented etc) as vars, and then mapping the most common symbols to operators
07:14:12 :quintopia!~quintopia@unaffiliated/quintopia PRIVMSG #esoteric :how is the size of befunge determined? non-whitespace?
07:14:29 :nrkn!3ceaa170@gateway/web/freenode/ip.60.234.161.112 PRIVMSG #esoteric :But it has to be reasonably high level to get a lot done, definitely not the case with brainfuck etc.
07:14:40 :fizzie!fis@iris.zem.fi PRIVMSG #esoteric :At least at anagolf it's determined like the others, which means it's a very bad idea to leave whitespace at the beginning of lines.
07:14:46 :Lymia!~moe@unaffiliated/cirno-chan PRIVMSG #esoteric ::s
07:14:52 :Lymia!~moe@unaffiliated/cirno-chan PRIVMSG #esoteric :Generation 12 running.
07:14:56 :quintopia!~quintopia@unaffiliated/quintopia PRIVMSG #esoteric :oh so all whitespace is significant?
07:14:58 :Lymia!~moe@unaffiliated/cirno-chan PRIVMSG #esoteric :God a hill size of 32 is slow.
07:15:05 :quintopia!~quintopia@unaffiliated/quintopia PRIVMSG #esoteric :i thought you were asleep lymia
07:15:10 :Lymia!~moe@unaffiliated/cirno-chan PRIVMSG #esoteric :I'm supposed to be.
07:15:17 :fizzie!fis@iris.zem.fi PRIVMSG #esoteric :quintopia: All bytes count, even the terminating newline if you sillily leave one in.
07:15:23 :quintopia!~quintopia@unaffiliated/quintopia PRIVMSG #esoteric :huh
07:15:24 :nrkn!3ceaa170@gateway/web/freenode/ip.60.234.161.112 PRIVMSG #esoteric :I don't use whitespace at all except that newlines are equiv to statement terminators, also semicolons, all whitespace ignored except in string literals
