07:22:48 :fizzie!fis@iris.zem.fi PRIVMSG #esoteric :Demoscene doesn't imply Windows anyway; we just took a look, and pouet has something like six or seven Solaris demos.
07:22:54 :zzo38!~zzo38@h24-207-49-17.dlt.dccnet.com PRIVMSG #esoteric :Demoscene is not always for Windows (or necessarily any other system). These demos have been written for many different systems, including NES and Pokemon Mini.
07:23:55 :nrkn!3ceaa170@gateway/web/freenode/ip.60.234.161.112 PRIVMSG #esoteric :Interesting how much demoscene stuff in the last (x) years has relied on OS API calls though
07:23:56 :pikhq!~pikhq@174-22-169-62.clsp.qwest.net PRIVMSG #esoteric :Isn't the demoscene *older* than Windows?
07:24:11 :quintopia!~quintopia@unaffiliated/quintopia PRIVMSG #esoteric :fizzie: how old?
07:24:13 :pikhq!~pikhq@174-22-169-62.clsp.qwest.net PRIVMSG #esoteric :nrkn: Just certain forms of demos.
07:24:26 :pikhq!~pikhq@174-22-169-62.clsp.qwest.net PRIVMSG #esoteric :nrkn: You can still find stuff like, say, C64 demos.
