13:00:03 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :what does y on positive do?
13:00:05 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :UNDEF?
13:00:10 :Deewiant!~deewiant@cs186230.pp.htv.fi PRIVMSG #esoteric :y on positive?
13:00:17 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :The y "Get SysInfo" instruction, only available in Funge-98, pops one value off the stack. If the value is zero or negative, y tells you far more than you ever really want to know about the underlying Funge interpreter, operating system, and computer (and is thus usually followed soon after by a n instruction).
13:00:24 :Deewiant!~deewiant@cs186230.pp.htv.fi PRIVMSG #esoteric :See below.
13:00:37 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :Oh :P
