15:15:11 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :Deewiant: Yes, but the name Ray doesn't.
15:15:13 :ais523!~ais523@unaffiliated/ais523 PRIVMSG #esoteric :Deewiant: I know, it's the name I was talking about
15:15:18 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :It's the same ray no matter how fast you're travelling.
15:15:45 :ais523!~ais523@unaffiliated/ais523 PRIVMSG #esoteric :elliott: it's just a fingerprint for INTERCAL control flow semantics
15:16:02 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :ais523: why on earth was it implemented by ... right, of course.
15:16:03 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric ::p
15:16:14 :ais523!~ais523@unaffiliated/ais523 PRIVMSG #esoteric :plus, an allowance for line numbers to be shared between the Funge program and a different program
15:16:16 :ais523!~ais523@unaffiliated/ais523 PRIVMSG #esoteric :which gives you an FFI
15:16:17 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :ais523: but you had an intercal->funge ffi, didn't you?
15:16:19 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :right
15:16:35 :ais523!~ais523@unaffiliated/ais523 PRIVMSG #esoteric :it's a useful fingerprint even if not used as an FFI, anyway
15:16:39 :ais523!~ais523@unaffiliated/ais523 PRIVMSG #esoteric :for certain values of "useful"
15:16:53 :ais523!~ais523@unaffiliated/ais523 PRIVMSG #esoteric :but the real merit is in hooking up other programs to the same control system
15:16:56 :Deewiant!~deewiant@cs186230.pp.htv.fi PRIVMSG #esoteric :Maybe I should write an INTERCAL interp so I could do IFFI
15:16:59 :ais523!~ais523@unaffiliated/ais523 PRIVMSG #esoteric :so you can jump around between them via COME FROM
15:17:15 :ais523!~ais523@unaffiliated/ais523 PRIVMSG #esoteric :and NEXT, etc
15:17:32 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :Deewiant: :D
15:17:42 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :Deewiant: does D not have an FFI? ;)
