16:07:47 :ais523!~ais523@unaffiliated/ais523 PRIVMSG #esoteric :elliott: doesn't Deewiant's # interpretation do that?
16:07:48 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :Therefore, after traversing the infinite Lahey space line magic, it arrives at the other side at (0,0).
16:07:53 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :ais523: Hmm, right.
16:08:00 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :I don't see how wrapping and # are any different, though.
16:08:01 :Deewiant!~deewiant@cs186230.pp.htv.fi PRIVMSG #esoteric :(0,0) is (2n,0) with n = 0.
16:08:04 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :I don't see how wrapping and # are any different, though.
16:08:17 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :Why does wrapping end up past the start of the line because of the delta, and # not?
16:08:26 :Deewiant!~deewiant@cs186230.pp.htv.fi PRIVMSG #esoteric :Huh?
16:08:30 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :loop (x,y) (dx,dy) (mx,my)
16:08:30 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :  | x `ltx` mx && y `lty` my = (mx+dx, my+dy)
16:08:31 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :From my loop.
16:08:36 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :i.e., for positive dx and dy:
16:08:40 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :if x < maximumx and y < maximumy
16:08:44 :Deewiant!~deewiant@cs186230.pp.htv.fi PRIVMSG #esoteric :# is just movement
16:08:47 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :er
16:08:47 :Deewiant!~deewiant@cs186230.pp.htv.fi PRIVMSG #esoteric :You wrap thereafter
16:08:48 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :*minimum
16:08:54 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :then resulting position is (minimum x + dx, minimum y + dy)
16:08:55 :Deewiant!~deewiant@cs186230.pp.htv.fi PRIVMSG #esoteric :You don't necessarily hit the start of the line
16:09:05 :Deewiant!~deewiant@cs186230.pp.htv.fi PRIVMSG #esoteric :But with a delta of (1,0) you of course do
16:09:49 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :Deewiant: Then I don't see why my interpretation of # as advance is wrong. Sure, it wraps but OHHH
16:10:01 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :It can advance, making it wrap, and will then go to the next instruction.
16:10:04 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :OK, I think I can fix that.
16:10:48 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :doCharIns '#' = modifyRay (\Ray (x,y) (dx,dy) -> (x+dx,y+dy))
16:10:49 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :TADA
16:10:55 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :BAD: 1k[ turns left at [
16:10:59 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :Baf
16:10:59 :Deewiant!~deewiant@cs186230.pp.htv.fi PRIVMSG #esoteric :# as advance is completely correct, it's just that the way you do wrapping with the bounds rectangle it works a bit weirdly
