16:17:27 :Deewiant!~deewiant@cs186230.pp.htv.fi PRIVMSG #esoteric :GOOD: , works can't rely on : working yet, so it can't use a loop.
16:17:46 :ais523!~ais523@unaffiliated/ais523 PRIVMSG #esoteric :flushes hardly slow down a program that isn't I/O bound anyway
16:17:48 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :Deewiant: ...That is amazing.
16:17:56 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :Deewiant: That is possibly my favourite slowdown ever.
16:17:59 :Deewiant!~deewiant@cs186230.pp.htv.fi PRIVMSG #esoteric :So it outputs at 1 char/tick instead of 1 char/7 ticks or so, I forget the loop's speed
16:18:05 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric ::-D
16:18:05 :ais523!~ais523@unaffiliated/ais523 PRIVMSG #esoteric :I use them in pretty much all my esolang interps, on the basis that esolangs are basically never I/O-bound
16:18:12 :Deewiant!~deewiant@cs186230.pp.htv.fi PRIVMSG #esoteric :If it's the right-to-left loop it's like 1 char/11 ticks
16:18:20 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :ais523: Befunge-98 IO is character-based, though.
16:18:30 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :So flushing is quite more dramatic than e.g. flushing after Underload's S :P
16:18:40 :Deewiant!~deewiant@cs186230.pp.htv.fi PRIVMSG #esoteric :Flushes aren't exactly zero-cost for CPU anyway.
16:18:48 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :Deewiant: I think my talk about no premature optimisation was a bit much.
16:18:55 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :How long is the typical Mycology output? :P
16:18:59 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :When fully passed.
16:18:59 :ais523!~ais523@unaffiliated/ais523 PRIVMSG #esoteric :Deewiant: no, but the length of time they take is proportional to the amount of I/O you do
16:19:12 :ais523!~ais523@unaffiliated/ais523 PRIVMSG #esoteric :so they hurt I/O-bound programs much more than CPU-bound programs
16:19:41 :ais523!~ais523@unaffiliated/ais523 PRIVMSG #esoteric :(this morning, I was learning about GPU-bound programs, and how they can either be memory-bound or thread-bound)
16:19:46 :elliott!~elliott@unaffiliated/elliott PRIVMSG #esoteric :There are plenty CPU-bound programs that do a lot of IO while computing. :P
